\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 Your order is right. One necessary adaptation: Kairo uses Fastify and users can belong to multiple companies, so tenant context cannot simply be copied from the login JWT. The user must select a company once; the API validates that selection server-side and issues/stores a trusted active context. Downstream routes must never accept tenant identity from headers, URL, query, or body.\
I would implement this as a security release, not as a broad rewrite.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

